  '0a237d4f-9ff1-496e-aae4-83b153770acd', 'CSCO-AID-ENT-001', 'ai-defense-enterprise', 'Cisco AI Defense for building and using enterprise AI', 'Cisco AI Defense for building and using enterprise AI',
  'public_announcement', 'primary_source', 'This is the 15 January 2025 Cisco announcement, not a named customer deployment. The 29 percent figure is Cisco''s citation of the 2024 AI Readiness Index, not a baseline for this pilot. Kent Noyes''s comment is a partner remark, not a measured result.', 'published', 'public',
  'Cisco announced AI Defense as one control layer for building AI and for using it. Development controls cover discovery of who is building which app, model validation, and runtime protection. Use controls cover shadow and approved AI, access limits, and ongoing protection of data. Splunk customers receive enriched alerts. A PM uses this record to freeze the vocabulary and the boundary of the product, then attaches a sector scenario when regulation or segmentation is in scope.', 'Cisco''s cited 2024 AI Readiness Index said only 29 percent of responding organizations were ready to detect and prevent unauthorized AI manipulation. AI apps span multiple models and clouds. Weaknesses sit in both the model and the application, and the owner may be a developer, a user, or a vendor. Point guardrails inside each model do not give one control.', 'The announcement describes network visibility as the common control layer, so development pipelines and employee use do not each depend on a separately bought point product. Cisco said enterprises could use the product from March 2025.', 'Separate the source card from the sector charter. This record fixes terms. A financial-services or data-center program cites it and does not copy it as that program''s result.', 'The organization leaves with two lists, user AI and developer AI, a detection log from the test scenarios, and a written decision on whether to expand. No savings figure is published.',
  'cross_industry', 'Cross-industry', 'enterprise', 'Enterprise', 'Global', array['NIST AI RMF', 'OWASP LLM Top 10', 'MITRE ATLAS'],
  'Enterprise', 'hybrid', 'Hybrid, with network enforcement points', 'Discovery, model validation, and runtime security for applications being built. Visibility, access control, and data protection for applications being used. Detection uses Talos. The product sits in Cisco Security Cloud and uses network enforcement points. Splunk enrichment applies only where the customer already has Splunk.', 'medium',
  'Amounts and durations are planning bands for a first subscription pilot. They are not a list price and not a customer result.', 250000, 1200000, 'M',
  4, 8, 8, 16,
  array['Cisco AI Defense', 'Cisco Security Cloud', 'Cisco Talos'], array['Splunk'], array['Shadow and approved AI discovery', 'Model validation', 'Runtime protection'], array['Access control', 'Data-loss controls', 'Enriched alerts for Splunk customers'], array['AI Defense', 'shadow AI', 'model validation', 'runtime protection', 'Security Cloud'],
  array['A list of user-facing AI and a separate list of AI being built', 'A written test set and the detection record', 'A decision on whether Splunk enrichment is in scope', 'A source note whenever the 29 percent figure is used'], array['Treating the partner comment as a deployment result', 'A data-center segmentation design, which belongs in the Hypershield financial scenario', 'Combining the developer approver and the employee-access approver into one person'], array['User AI and developer AI are separate lists', 'The test scenarios leave a detection record', 'Expansion is a separate decision'], 'published', array['Published fact, 15 January 2025: Cisco described discovery of shadow and approved AI, model validation, runtime protection, access control, and data protection as one solution.', 'Published fact: Cisco said it participates in related MITRE, OWASP, and NIST work.', 'Published fact: Splunk customers receive enriched alerts. That sentence does not apply to a customer without Splunk.'],
