) values (
  '6a1f505b-a8be-4fea-a086-6a30326ea6ff', 'CSCO-WX-AIM-001', 'webex-specialized-models', 'Governance plan for Webex specialized models and security-product LLM use', 'Governance plan for Webex specialized models and security-product LLM use',
  'reference_scenario', 'public_composite', 'Noise removal, virtual backgrounds, gestures, and the responsible-AI notes are public Cisco Live and transparency descriptions. The security-product LLM pattern is the prompt-tuning and expert-review pattern in the public XDR material. A procedure for training a foundation model on customer content is not public and is not in this case. Amounts and durations are planning bands.', 'published', 'public',
  'Turning on Webex AI features needs a per-feature data-flow table before a single policy. Cisco''s public notes say noise removal runs on the device, virtual backgrounds were trained across lighting and groups and then tested for bias, and gesture recognition uses a model from consented internal data. Meeting summaries and a security-product LLM are a different path: prompts, a proxy, and a person. The default is that customer content is not used to train the model.', 'Switching collaboration AI on as one feature mixes privacy, bias, and meeting content leaving for an external model. A security team that says it will build its own LLM then has a project with no data rights and no evaluation. Each feature moves data differently, and the policy is still one page.', 'Cisco''s public material separates, by feature, an AI impact assessment, training-data review, on-device processing, and a security LLM proxy. A PM can turn that separation into requirements and tests.', 'Features with a published on-device path can be piloted first. Anything that sends content to a model waits for the data-flow row and the impact assessment.', 'The organization keeps a list of features that may be on and features that need more review. The security LLM is not wired to an automatic action before an evaluation set exists.',
  'workplace', 'Collaboration', 'enterprise', 'Enterprise', 'Global', array['Privacy notice', 'Biometric-information caution', 'AI impact assessment'],
  'Enterprise', 'hybrid', 'On-device processing and a controlled cloud LLM', 'Noise removal on the device. Virtual backgrounds as on-device inference plus a local user image. Meeting-summary LLMs pass input and output guardrails and a security proxy, and the public note says content is not kept for training. A security-product LLM is a tuned prompt on incident data plus human review.', 'medium',
  'Amounts and durations are planning bands for a collaboration program. They are not a list price.', 150000, 800000, 'M',
  4, 8, 10, 20,
  array['Webex', 'Webex AI', 'Cisco AI security proxy'], array[]::text[], array['On-device noise removal', 'Virtual backgrounds', 'Gesture recognition', 'Meeting LLM summary', 'Security incident summary prompt'], array['Per-feature data flow', 'No training on customer content by default', 'Human review before a security action'], array['Webex', 'noise removal', 'virtual background', 'gesture', 'LLM', 'bias'],
  array['A data-flow row per feature', 'An acceptance test where Cisco has published a bias or audio-range gap', 'User notice and administrator settings', 'For the security LLM, a prompt version and an evaluation set'], array['Training a foundation model on customer meetings', 'One policy that covers on-device and cloud features', 'Automatic containment from a security summary'], array['The per-feature data-flow table is approved', 'Bias and audio-range acceptance tests are recorded where Cisco published a gap', 'The security LLM is not connected to an automatic action without an evaluation set'], 'published', array['Public description: Cisco Live material says noise-removal processing happens on the device, so that feature does not send the audio to the cloud.', 'Public description: early virtual backgrounds varied by hairstyle, skin tone, and lighting, and noise removal varied in the higher register. Cisco says later data and tests closed the gaps.', 'Public description: Webex does not by default train models on customer content. It uses licensed, internal, and synthetic data, and runs an AI impact assessment per feature.'],
  null, null, '2023-06-01'
);
