insert into case_chunks (id, case_id, chunk_index, section, heading, content, token_estimate, embedding) values ('32500bd4-a156-4963-aaac-430b68907b3d', '6a1f505b-a8be-4fea-a086-6a30326ea6ff', 5, 'scope', 'Scope, assumptions, and constraints (1)', 'case: CSCO-WX-AIM-001
title: Governance plan for Webex specialized models and security-product LLM use
industry: Collaboration (workplace)
segment: Enterprise
solutions: Webex, Webex AI, Cisco AI security proxy
partners: 
aliases: Webex, noise removal, virtual background, gesture, LLM, bias
fidelity: public_composite
In scope
- A data-flow row per feature
- An acceptance test where Cisco has published a bias or audio-range gap
- User notice and administrator settings
- For the security LLM, a prompt version and an evaluation set

Out of scope
- Training a foundation model on customer meetings
- One policy that covers on-device and cloud features
- Automatic containment from a security summary

Assumptions
- The security LLM track shares the operating model with the XDR case and keeps its own schedule. (owner: Customer PM, status: open)
- Privacy will review the impact assessment before a cloud feature is enabled. (owner: Privacy, status: open)

Constraints
- [contractual] The default written into the pilot is that customer content is not used to train the model.
