title: Governance plan for Webex specialized models and security-product LLM use
industry: Collaboration (workplace)
segment: Enterprise
solutions: Webex, Webex AI, Cisco AI security proxy
partners: 
aliases: Webex, noise removal, virtual background, gesture, LLM, bias
fidelity: public_composite
1 Feature list [Initiating/Scope] owner Collaboration admin, 3–5 days, deliverable: List. Name noise removal, backgrounds, gestures, summaries, and the security LLM as separate rows.
2.1 Data-flow table [Planning/AI governance] owner Privacy, 8–12 days, deliverable: Table. For each row, write where data is processed and whether it is used for training.
2.2 User notice [Planning/Communications] owner Legal, 5–8 days, deliverable: Notice. The notice matches the table. Biometric caution is explicit for gestures.
2.3 Evaluation set [Planning/Security] owner Security operations lead, 8–12 days, deliverable: Evaluation set. The security LLM gets a prompt version and a set of incidents a person will score.
3.1 On-device pilot [Executing/Quality] owner Collaboration admin, 10–15 days, deliverable: Pilot note. Enable noise removal for a named group. Confirm the table''s on-device row.
3.2 Acceptance tests [Executing/Quality] owner Privacy, 5–10 days, deliverable: Test note. Record the bias and audio-range checks Cisco''s material says were the gaps.
