1 Pilot charter [Initiating/Scope] owner Internal IT PM, 5–8 days, deliverable: Charter. Name the hall or pod. Write the few-week rule in one sentence.
2.1 Fiber survey [Planning/Quality] owner Network operations, 10–15 days, deliverable: Survey. Sample the spans. Mark which ones are dual multimode.
2.2 Standard design [Planning/Integration] owner Network operations, 10–20 days, deliverable: Standard. Fix Silicon One, NOS, dashboard, and telemetry scope.
2.3 Order [Planning/Procurement] owner Internal IT PM, 10–20 days, deliverable: Orders. Order only the equipment the survey supports.
3.1 Pilot turn-up [Executing/Schedule] owner Network operations, 30–50 days, deliverable: Turn-up checklist. Open the pod in the existing change window, 6 to 10 weeks after arrival.
3.2 Policy rehearsal [Executing/Security] owner Security architect, 5–10 days, deliverable: Rehearsal note. Switch a test policy on the dual data plane and roll it back.
4 Handover [Monitoring and controlling/Communications] owner Network operations, 5–8 days, deliverable: Runbook page. The runbook names the pod. No whole-hall claim.
