insert into case_chunks (id, case_id, chunk_index, section, heading, content, token_estimate, embedding) values ('d675209c-e037-413d-abd6-a08b32ed3588', 'c0445a81-159a-4efb-a7a1-4c850784412b', 4, 'scope', 'Scope, assumptions, and constraints (1)', 'case: CSCO-XDR-SOC-001
title: AI-assisted security operations with Cisco XDR
industry: Cross-industry (cross_industry)
segment: Security operations
solutions: Cisco XDR, Cisco Talos, Cisco Secure Access, Splunk SOAR
partners: 
aliases: XDR, SOC, Instant Attack Verification, incident summary, agentic SOC
fidelity: primary_source
In scope
- An evaluation set of past incidents
- A rule that high-impact containment needs a person
- A comparison of the draft summary with the evidence
- A note that the CiscoKorea video is a demo

Out of scope
- Pasting the video click-path into the runbook
- A time-saved percentage
- Unattended isolation
- Foundation-model training on customer incidents

Assumptions
- The SOC already has a containment playbook. This pilot does not invent one. (owner: SOC lead, status: open)
- Splunk SOAR is in scope only if it is already the automation tool. (owner: Customer PM, status: open)

Constraints
- [organizational] A high-impact action without a named person is a failed test, not a faster one.
