insert into case_chunks (id, case_id, chunk_index, section, heading, content, token_estimate, embedding) values ('c120149b-1945-469e-a970-8047d28b73bd', 'c0445a81-159a-4efb-a7a1-4c850784412b', 8, 'wbs', 'WBS', 'case: CSCO-XDR-SOC-001
title: AI-assisted security operations with Cisco XDR
industry: Cross-industry (cross_industry)
segment: Security operations
solutions: Cisco XDR, Cisco Talos, Cisco Secure Access, Splunk SOAR
partners: 
aliases: XDR, SOC, Instant Attack Verification, incident summary, agentic SOC
fidelity: primary_source
1 Approval rule [Initiating/Security] owner SOC lead, 3–5 days, deliverable: Rule. Write that high-impact containment needs a person. Name the actions that count as high impact.
2.1 Incident set [Planning/Quality] owner SOC lead, 5–10 days, deliverable: Set. Pick past incidents. Record the evidence a good summary must mention.
2.2 Playbook review [Planning/Risk] owner Automation owner, 5–8 days, deliverable: Playbook note. Confirm SOAR has no path from the draft to isolation.
2.3 Demo note [Planning/Communications] owner Customer PM, 1–2 days, deliverable: Note. Cite the CiscoKorea video as a demo. Forbid timestamp steps in the runbook.
3.1 Draft and score [Executing/Quality] owner Incident responder, 10–15 days, deliverable: Score sheet. Generate summaries for the set. A person accepts or rejects each one.
3.2 Verification check [Executing/Security] owner Detection engineer, 5–8 days, deliverable: Check note. Where Instant Attack Verification is available, record that it is a check and not the approver.
4 Action audit [Monitoring and controlling/Security] owner Automation owner, 3–5 days, deliverable: Audit. Review the pilot window for unattended containment.
