  '9ad6f613-79ae-4ab1-a1d9-e6b050a39e9c', 'IND-DEERE-SPRAY-001', 'john-deere-see-and-spray', 'John Deere See & Spray targeted herbicide application', 'John Deere See & Spray targeted herbicide application',
  'public_announcement', 'primary_source', 'Figures are John Deere''s published claims from the 18 September 2024 release, including the Iowa State University study as Deere cites it. This record does not re-audit acreage, gallons, or the study. The release''s footnotes say individual results vary.', 'published', 'public',
  'See & Spray uses boom-mounted cameras and onboard processors to spray herbicide only where a weed is recognized. John Deere''s 18 September 2024 release says customers saved an estimated 8 million gallons of herbicide mix on more than 1 million acres in the 2024 season, with an average 59 percent herbicide savings on corn, soybean, and cotton in the United States. Cameras scan over 2,100 square feet per second at up to 15 mph. Customers pay for the acres where the technology is used. A PM copying this pattern separates those published figures from a grower''s own as-applied maps.', 'Broadcast spraying puts herbicide on crop and on bare ground, not only on weeds. That spends chemical, water, and stops, and it is a poor fit for a stewardship target. A camera system that cannot show where it sprayed leaves the grower with a vendor percentage and no field record.', 'See & Spray, introduced in 2021, opens individual ExactApply nozzles when cameras and processors class a plant as a weed. Deere''s release says the 2024 season covered corn, soybean, cotton, and fallow, and that an Iowa State University study it cites found 76 percent average product savings and 15.70 US dollars per acre economic savings on the study fields. In 2025 Deere said it would introduce an Application Savings Guarantee so customers pay for the technology when application savings are there.', 'Treat the machine as a measurement system as well as a sprayer. The Operations Center map is the evidence. The press percentage is the manufacturer''s season claim.', 'A grower or custom applicator can compare as-applied maps with a broadcast baseline on the same fields. The 59 percent and the 8 million gallons are Deere''s 2024 season figures, not a promise for the next field.',
  'agriculture', 'Agriculture', 'grower', 'Growers and custom applicators', 'United States', array['FIFRA label compliance', 'State pesticide records', 'USDA conservation program rules where relevant'],
  'Farm or retail applicator', 'on_prem', 'On-machine cameras, processors, and nozzles, with Operations Center maps', 'Boom cameras scan the crop, onboard processors class crop versus weed, ExactApply nozzles spray only the recognized weed, and John Deere Operations Center stores the as-applied map against a broadcast comparison.', 'medium',
  'Amounts and durations below are planning bands for a similar program. They are not the publisher''s result and not a price quote.', 150000, 900000, 'M',
  8, 20, 12, 30,
  array['See & Spray', 'ExactApply', 'John Deere Operations Center'], array[]::text[], array['Camera-based crop versus weed classification', 'Per-nozzle spray decisions', 'As-applied mapping'], array['Machine and account access control', 'Retention of application records'], array['See and Spray', 'herbicide', 'targeted spray', 'corn', 'soybean', 'cotton', 'fallow'],
  array['One sprayer platform and the crops the installed software supports', 'A season plan that records acres, mix, and the broadcast comparison', 'Operator training on when targeted mode is exited', 'A readout that cites Deere''s 2024 figures separately from this farm''s maps'], array['Treating 59 percent as this farm''s target before a season of maps', 'Using the system on a crop the installed release does not support', 'Ignoring the release footnotes on weed pressure, speed, and settings'], array['As-applied maps exist for the season''s See & Spray acres', 'Broadcast comparison is visible for those acres', 'Operators can say when they left targeted mode'], 'published', array['Publisher claim, John Deere, 18 September 2024: an estimated 8 million gallons of herbicide mix saved on more than 1 million acres in the 2024 season.', 'Publisher claim, same release: average herbicide savings of 59 percent on corn, soybean, and cotton fields across the United States. The release says individual results vary.', 'Publisher description, same release: cameras scan over 2,100 square feet per second at up to 15 mph, and ExactApply nozzles spray only where a weed is recognized.', 'Publisher citation, same release: an Iowa State University study showed 76 percent average product savings and 15.70 US dollars per acre on the study fields. This record does not re-analyze that study.'],
  null, null, '2024-09-18'
);
