  '12c1b276-5b40-43f8-a8b5-3c826612f17d', 'IND-MOD-MRNA-001', 'moderna-mrna-design-on-aws', 'Moderna mRNA design and the AWS digital platform', 'Moderna mRNA design and the AWS digital platform',
  'public_announcement', 'primary_source', 'Two AWS pages state the early COVID-19 timeline differently. The 5 August 2020 AWS press release says the first clinical batch of mRNA-1273 reached NIH 42 days after the virus was sequenced. A later AWS case-study page says the sequence was completed in 2 days with machine learning on AWS and the first clinical batch was released 25 days later. Both sentences are stored. They are not merged into one number.', 'published', 'public',
  'Moderna runs its Drug Design Studio and manufacturing data path on AWS. Public AWS accounts describe a digital loop from sequence design, through machine learning, to an automated preclinical plant. The COVID-19 timeline is published in two forms, 42 days and 25 days, and this record keeps both with their sources. A PM using the story plans a design-to-batch path, a human quality review, and a citation rule so the two timelines are never collapsed.', 'mRNA constructs used to take years to reach even preclinical work. Sequence choice, compute, lab execution, and quality review sat in different systems. Cryo-EM and other instruments add tens of terabytes a day. A single heroic timeline in a slide hides which source said 25 days and which said 42.', 'AWS describes Drug Design Studio on AWS: scientists pick proteins, algorithms propose mRNA sequences, jobs run through a queue and EC2, and an automated plant can make up to 1,000 constructs a month. The 5 August 2020 AWS release says Moderna selected AWS as its preferred cloud and standard for analytics and machine learning, and that the first clinical batch of mRNA-1273 went to NIH for Phase 1 42 days after sequencing. The case-study page states the 2-day sequence and 25-day batch. A 2017 AWS case quotes Marcello Damiani that a Zika vaccine candidate reached clinical trials in a year, against years in a traditional path.', 'The platform is the asset. A pandemic timeline is a published example with a source note, not a service level for the next program.', 'Scientists can order a construct and reach preclinical experiments in weeks rather than years, which is how Damiani described the 2017 studio. The organization can show a regulator or partner which source supports which day count.',
  'life_sciences', 'Life sciences', 'biopharma', 'Biopharma research and early manufacturing', 'Global', array['FDA IND and GMP expectations', 'GLP where nonclinical work requires it', 'Data integrity for electronic records'],
  'Biopharma', 'cloud', 'AWS for design, data, and manufacturing analytics', 'Drug Design Studio proposes sequences, batch jobs move through a queue to compute, results return to the studio, and an automated plant makes the physical mRNA. Instrument data is centralized before a scientist trusts it. Quality review stays with a person.', 'very_high',
  'Amounts and durations below are planning bands for a similar program. They are not the publisher''s result and not a price quote.', 1000000, 8000000, 'L',
  8, 16, 16, 40,
  array['Drug Design Studio', 'Automated mRNA manufacturing', 'AWS analytics and machine learning'], array['Amazon Web Services'], array['Sequence design', 'Machine learning on experimental results', 'Automated quality-control review support'], array['Partitioned research and manufacturing accounts', 'Audit trail on sequence release', 'Human release of a clinical batch'], array['Moderna', 'mRNA', 'mRNA-1273', 'Drug Design Studio', 'AWS', 'vaccine design'],
  array['One new sequence program from design ticket to preclinical batch', 'A citation sheet for the 2-day, 25-day, and 42-day statements', 'Human quality release before a batch is called clinical', 'A data path for instrument files into a single store'], array['Promising either 25 or 42 days for a future pathogen', 'Using the COVID-19 timeline as a manufacturing SLA', 'Skipping QA release because the studio job finished'], array['The citation sheet lists both AWS wordings with URLs', 'The pilot program has a design ticket, a batch record, and a quality release', 'Instrument data for the pilot lands in one store before analysis'], 'published', array['AWS press release, 5 August 2020: Moderna delivered the first clinical batch of mRNA-1273 to NIH for the Phase 1 trial 42 days after the initial sequencing of the virus.', 'AWS case-study page: Moderna completed the mRNA COVID-19 vaccine sequence in 2 days using machine learning on AWS, and the first clinical batch was released 25 days later.', 'AWS 2017 case study: the automated preclinical plant can create as many as 1,000 mRNA constructs a month, and Damiani said a Zika candidate reached clinical trials in a year.'],
  null, null, '2020-08-05'
);
